---
import Issuance from './Issuance.astro';
import Adopters from './Adopters.astro';
import release from '../data/release.json';
---
<div class="home-content not-content">
  <Adopters />
  <div class="principles">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">The problem</p><h2>How does a service know who is calling?</h2><p>When a workload makes a request, the receiving service needs to establish its identity. An IP address or hostname alone does not authenticate the caller. Passwords and API keys copied into deployments must be distributed and replaced wherever they are used.</p></div>
    <div><p class="eyebrow">The model</p><h2>SPIFFE IDs and SVIDs</h2><p>A SPIFFE ID names a workload within a trust domain. An SVID provides verifiable evidence of that identity. Workloads obtain these credentials through a local API.</p></div>
    <div><p class="eyebrow">The result</p><h2>Authentication between services</h2><p>The receiving service authenticates the caller and applies its own authorization policy. The identity can remain the same across deployments.</p></div>
  </div>
  <Issuance />
  <section class="primitives section-block" aria-labelledby="primitives-heading">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / Concepts</p><h2 id="primitives-heading">SPIFFE concepts</h2></div></div>
    <div class="primitive-grid">
      <a href="/docs/spiffe/specs/spiffe-id/"><span class="primitive-number">01</span><h3>SPIFFE ID <span>↗</span></h3><p>A URI that names a workload within a trust domain.</p><code>spiffe://example.org/payments</code></a>
      <a href="/docs/spiffe/specs/x509-svid/"><span class="primitive-number">02</span><h3>SVID <span>↗</span></h3><p>A verifiable identity document that binds a SPIFFE ID to a key or token.</p><code>X.509-SVID · JWT-SVID</code></a>
      <a href="/docs/spiffe/specs/workload-api/"><span class="primitive-number">03</span><h3>Workload API <span>↗</span></h3><p>A local interface for obtaining SVIDs and trust bundles.</p><code>FetchX509SVID</code></a>
      <a href="/docs/spiffe/specs/trust-domain-and-bundle/"><span class="primitive-number">04</span><h3>Trust domain <span>↗</span></h3><p>An administrative boundary with its own issuing authority.</p><code>example.org</code></a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="usecases section-block" aria-labelledby="usecases-heading">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / Applications</p><h2 id="usecases-heading">Workload authentication</h2></div></div>
    <div class="usecase-row"><span class="row-number">01</span><h3>Mutual TLS between services</h3><p>Use X.509-SVIDs to authenticate both ends of a connection. Authorize the peer by its SPIFFE ID.</p></div>
    <div class="usecase-row"><span class="row-number">02</span><h3>Authentication to platforms</h3><p>Present an SVID to a compatible service, or exchange it for platform credentials with a scoped lifetime.</p></div>
    <div class="usecase-row"><span class="row-number">03</span><h3>Federation between trust domains</h3><p>Exchange public trust bundles so independently operated domains can verify each other's identities.</p></div>
  </section>
  <section class="project-pair section-block" aria-labelledby="projects-heading">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">04 / The standard and its implementation</p><h2 id="projects-heading">SPIFFE and SPIRE</h2></div></div>
    <div class="project-pair-grid">
      <div><img class="project-logo" src="/img/logos/spiffe/horizontal/color/spiffe-horizontal-color.svg" alt="SPIFFE" width="154" height="52" /><span class="project-kind">THE STANDARD</span><h3>The workload identity standard</h3><p>SPIFFE defines how identities are named and represented, how workloads obtain them, and how trust domains interoperate.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/spiffe/specs/">Read the specifications →</a></div>
      <div><img class="project-logo" src="/img/logos/spire/horizontal/color/spire-horizontal-color.svg" alt="SPIRE" width="154" height="52" /><span class="project-kind">THE REFERENCE IMPLEMENTATION</span><h3>Workload identity with SPIRE</h3><p>SPIRE attests nodes and workloads, issues SVIDs, and rotates them. It is community governed, with contributors across organizations.</p><div class="inline-links"><a class="text-link" href="/spire/">SPIRE overview →</a><a class="release-link" href="/downloads/">{release.tag}</a></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="ecosystem-preview section-block" aria-labelledby="ecosystem-heading">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">05 / An open ecosystem</p><h2 id="ecosystem-heading">SPIFFE implementations and integrations</h2></div><p>Find identity issuers, application libraries, and services that accept SPIFFE identities.</p></div>
    <div class="ecosystem-names"><a href="/spire/">SPIRE</a><a href="/ecosystem/">Teleport</a><a href="/ecosystem/">Istio</a><a href="/ecosystem/">Consul</a><a href="/ecosystem/">cert-manager</a><a href="/ecosystem/">Envoy</a></div>
    <div class="inline-links"><a class="text-link" href="/ecosystem/">Explore the ecosystem →</a></div>
  </section>
  <section class="resources section-block" aria-labelledby="resources-heading">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">06 / Resources</p><h2 id="resources-heading">Learn about SPIFFE</h2></div></div>
    <div class="resource-grid"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q2SiGeebRKY"><span class="resource-type">WATCH / 10 MINUTES</span><h3>Introduction to SPIFFE</h3><p>The problem, the identity model, and where SPIRE fits.</p><span class="text-link">Watch the introduction ↗</span></a><a href="/book/"><span class="resource-type">READ / THE SPIFFE BOOK</span><h3>Solving the Bottom Turtle.</h3><p>Designing and operating workload identity in distributed systems.</p><span class="text-link">Read the book →</span></a><a href="/community/"><span class="resource-type">PARTICIPATE / COMMUNITY</span><h3>SPIFFE community</h3><p>Meetings, discussions, and contribution guidelines.</p><span class="text-link">Community resources →</span></a></div>
  </section>
  <div class="cncf-strip"><img src="/img/logos/cncf-color.png" alt="Cloud Native Computing Foundation" width="148" height="48" /><p>SPIFFE and SPIRE are CNCF graduated projects.</p><a href="https://www.cncf.io/projects/spiffe/">Project information ↗</a></div>
</div>
